description: Rules for JavaScript (jQuery 3.6, Axios) in a non-SPA, multi-page app.
globs: ["resources/js/**/*.js", "public/**/*.js"]
alwaysApply: true

# General
- Prefer modular, isolated scripts per-page/feature; avoid global namespace pollution.
- Use IIFE or modules via Vite for scoping where possible.
- Handle errors (try/catch or .catch); avoid silent failures.
- Use Axios for HTTP; centralize Axios config (base URL, CSRF headers).

# jQuery
- Use event delegation for dynamic content.
- Avoid deep DOM traversal and brittle selectors; use data-* attributes for hooks.
- Do not inject large HTML strings in JS; prefer Blade partials or small templates.
- Avoid mixing unrelated concerns in a single file.

# Performance
- Throttle/debounce expensive handlers (scroll/resize).
- Avoid forced synchronous layouts; batch DOM reads/writes.

# Code Style
- Prefer const/let over var.
- Avoid files > ~300 lines; split by feature/module.
